  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $3$ and $7.$ We can make a common denominator of $3\\times 7=21.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $7$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $3$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/d9fdbf9a9f569024446f1be9866d51d32cd77dd69868b6efc30b16a7266abb50.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{21}÷\\frac{15}{21}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n14÷15=\\frac{14}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{14}{15}.\n$$",
